<title>FINLAND: PENOPE PROPOSES FIM 1.00 '96 DIVIDEND.</title>
<headline>PENOPE PROPOSES FIM 1.00 '96 DIVIDEND.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish wood machinery wholesaler Penope Oy on Thursday said it would propose a 1.00 markka dividend out of 1996 earnings, released earlier.</p>
<p>&quot;The board of directors of Penope will propose to the annual general meeting on April 9, 1997, that out of 1996 earnings ... a 1.00 markka dividend be paid on all 840,000 shares,&quot; the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>On February 27, Penope reported 1996 profit before appropriatins and taxes down 76 percent to 1.2 million markka from 4.8 million in 1995.</p>
<p>--Helsinki Newsroom +358-9-680 50 235</p>
